WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.619 --> 00:00:03.608
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.608 --> 00:00:04.710
(audience cheering)

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.080
- I'm not just saying it when I say, like,

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.100
I really believe that.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.440
I think you're just one of
the most prolific songwriters

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.330
of our generation and
you're so underrated.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.710
I know you've been nominated 17 times.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.080
I know people know. But like not enough.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.700
I think you're so gifted.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.700
And your voice is like quintessential,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.190
like, why I loved country
music growing up like that.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.690
It's perfect singer-songwriter.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.070
Your tone. There's no one like it.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.320
You know it's you, right
when you start singing.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.630
It's amazing and congratulations

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.712
on six nominations at the Grammys.

00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:34.658
(audience applauding)

00:00:34.658 --> 00:00:36.660
- I word vomit every time I see you.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.310
- Well, it means so much coming from you

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.540
'cause you're so great.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.490
- Oh, whatever. You're nice.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:45.270
- You really are and so to
hear you say that means a lot.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.790
- Oh, well, the felling is
mutual. I have to ask this.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.411
Being one of the openly gay
people in country music,

00:00:50.411 --> 00:00:52.380
that's hard in that industry.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.050
Like, I know even for Shane,
who's our mutual friend

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.520
that you did "Shucked" with, that was hard

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.360
for him in the beginning.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.860
Like, you know, 'cause
he was his own artist

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.090
and it was hard to get in the door.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.290
Now he's like one of the best songwriters.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.506
But like, do you feel
supported in the industry?

00:01:03.506 --> 00:01:05.130
- I do.
- That's great.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.080
- Yes, I do and I even think of a song

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.830
like "Dear Insecurity,"
how far things have come in

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.050
that last verse when I say
"she's really sure of me."

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:17.070
I never even thought of
saying "he," that's how far

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.420
I feel like not only I've come,

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.947
but the world has come that nobody said,

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.260
"Oh, maybe you should say he."

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.240
- Exactly 'cause previously people

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.220
that we both know in the
country music industry

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.800
that are not openly gay, like, it's hard.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.300
And there people would
tell them, "Don't do that.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.310
It'll shut off a whole,
an entire fan base.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.650
And it will kill your career, maybe."

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.960
And I think it's beautiful
that you feel comfortable

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.460
and you didn't, it wasn't
even like a thought.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.387
You were like, well this is me.

00:01:39.387 --> 00:01:41.520
- So, and I had all those same concerns.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.560
You know, Shane and I
are around the same age

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.880
and came up in the same time.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.530
But I just, I knew not
being me would kill myself.

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:51.180
And so, you know.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.013
- You gotta do.

00:01:52.013 --> 00:01:54.510
Yeah. I think it's such a
great thing too for other,

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:55.590
have you ever heard from other

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.670
artists that are younger than you?

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.970
- I have, in fact, I had a
moment that really touched me.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:03.270
Brook Eden, she came
out and she got married

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:04.380
and had this beautiful wedding,

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.970
I think it was in People Magazine.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:08.085
And I texted her to congratulate her about

00:02:08.085 --> 00:02:10.050
being so authentic.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.270
And she said to me, "You being

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.730
you has made it easier for me to be me."

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.608
And that really, it hits me now.

00:02:16.608 --> 00:02:17.693
- The greatest compliment ever.

00:02:17.693 --> 00:02:20.820
- Because you never think that
you're making a difference

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:21.900
in that way.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.558
- You're just doing you.

00:02:23.558 --> 00:02:25.020
- Yes, exactly. And that really,

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.150
really clearly, I'm
getting teary right now.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.770
- I know. No, I am too.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:31.110
Anytime I see someone cry,
I'm like, it's contagious.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.240
I'm like, oh my God, I'll cry with you.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.520
So, congratulations,
"Shucked" is incredible.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.350
And I have literally been in the process

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:39.300
'cause I've heard from Shane
like the whole time too.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.560
Like it's evolved

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.480
and it's been like a
decade in the planning.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.270
- We've always had a
dream of you being in it.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.758
- Oh my God. He said it first. I go,

00:02:47.758 --> 00:02:48.960
I cannot live in New York right now.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.040
Like when y'all first started doing it.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.620
And now I live in New York, but yeah.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.880
- That's always been a dream of ours.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.250
- But, well, just so you know,
I'm such a huge fan of it.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.320
It is so great. The music is so great.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.900
I mean, Tony Award
nominated. That's incredible.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.960
Did you ever think that
would happen in your career?

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.600
- No. It was a bucket list
for me to write a musical.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:07.590
But it was one of those things

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.450
that I always thought
was way down the road.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.850
And so it came around at a beautiful time

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:12.990
because when Shane

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.480
and I jumped in, we were
both so naive to this world.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.610
We didn't know it was gonna take 10 years.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.560
So, you know, you start
looking at your life

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.450
and you're like, how many
more of these do I have in me?

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.190
So I'm glad we started when we did

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.810
because we both loved it.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.100
And man,

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.200
there were times I didn't
think it was gonna open an

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.850
Envelope at different times.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.740
much less open on Broadway.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.800
So it was a real, it's been a
real testament to persistence.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.990
And he and Robert Horn who wrote the book

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:39.960
and myself, our friendship,
we're like family.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:43.440
- Yeah, well after 10
years, it's a lot of work.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.190
Hope you like him. It's
like hanging out a lot.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.560
So this last album, I
think we can both relate.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.760
My last album was very personal.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:51.960
Probably my most personal, and this

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.550
is very personal for you.

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:56.880
And it's, I think the,
I love all your albums.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.380
I've been such a fan,

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.210
but I do love that you've like, kind

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.070
of broke the walls on
several of these songs

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.180
and really let people in.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.830
I feel like you've kind of
always been that artist,

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.360
but it feels like the next level.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.710
Do you feel like that with this album?

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.750
- I do. And when I was doing it,

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.970
I didn't even realize
that's what I was doing.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.197
You know, someone at my
label pointed out to me like,

00:04:14.197 --> 00:04:16.080
"This is your most personal album."

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.970
And I said, "Really?" And he said, "Yeah.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:19.950
I mean, a song like 'Dear Insecurity.'

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.590
Like, you're being
vulnerable about yourself,

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.617
not about a relationship
with anyone but yourself."

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.470
- Really holding yourself accountable.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.480
- I'm really proud that you know,

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.030
that this album ended up doing that.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.080
And then like you said,

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.368
the production, the
production's so vulnerable

00:04:36.368 --> 00:04:38.190
that it's just, you're naked.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:40.680
- Well let's do another commercial break.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.020
Brandy's latest multi Grammy nominated

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.430
album is called "Brandy Clark."

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.070
If you don't win one of
those, I'm gonna protest.

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:47.903
It's out now.

00:04:47.903 --> 00:04:50.580
I'm like nominated 17
times. Come on y'all.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.530
She's up for six of 'em. I'm like, God.

00:04:53.494 --> 00:04:55.961
Anyway, I'll be voting for you.

